    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the offensive engine is anchored by our high-speed outfield contingent. **Corbin Carroll** (74.71) is our premier start, capitalizing on an ideal #2 spot and a dynamic platoon advantage against Bryce Miller. Joining him at the top of the board is **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.64), who benefits from a stellar 14% boost due to his platoon matchup against Jack Leiter, and **James Wood** (73.33), whose lead-off role against Canning and strong xwOBA profile make him an elite producer. **Brice Turang** (70.37) and **Jose Caballero** (69.24) also provide excellent efficiency; the latter is particularly well-positioned for a productive day, as his score is inflated by a 10% park factor boost and a significant 13% platoon edge against the southpaw Jacob Lopez.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley**, whose 53.37 score nearly earned him a spot in the starting rotation. While he possesses the talent to outperform his projection, the combination of a tough matchup against Lodolo and limited platoon upside kept him on the pine in favor of more efficient, optimized slots. We are also maintaining a cautious approach regarding **Dalton Rushing** (53.28) and **Alex Freeland** (48.37), both of whom are currently tagged as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should either fall out of their assumed batting orders, their efficiency scores\u2014already hampered by bottom-of-the-order placement\u2014would plummet further, making them candidates for late-day pivots if better options emerge from the waiver wire.\n\nRegarding risk management, we are keeping a close eye on the volatile matchups for **Henry Bolte** (49.63) and **Seiya Suzuki** (58.32). **Henry Bolte** is facing a difficult R/R platoon disadvantage, which is currently suppressing his output, and we are monitoring the weather in his park to ensure no late-breaking threats to his availability. Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** fell just below our 40.0 floor at 39.92; despite his lead-off positioning, the negative platoon impact against Suarez made him an easy exclusion for today\u2019s aggressive lineup strategy. With **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, we remain heavily weighted toward stolen base upside to maintain our categorical dominance.",
